    "steps": [
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 93,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 94,
        "char_start": 0,
        "effective_step": 1,
        "end_token_index": 27,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 28,
        "step_number": 1,
        "text": "Step 1: Calculate the distance between points \\(C\\) and \\(D\\). Given that \\(CD = 140\\) meters."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 351,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 352,
        "char_start": 96,
        "effective_step": 2,
        "end_token_index": 120,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 121,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: Use the Pythagorean theorem to find the distance \\(OC\\) and \\(OD\\). Since \\(O\\) is the origin and \\(C\\) and \\(D\\) are directly south and east of \\(O\\) respectively, we have:\n\\[ OC = OD = \\sqrt{140^2 / 2} = \\sqrt{9800} = 70\\sqrt{2} \\text{ meters} \\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 465,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 466,
        "char_start": 354,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 159,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 160,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: Calculate the lengths of the ropes \\(HC\\) and \\(HD\\). Given \\(HC = 150\\) meters and \\(HD = 130\\) meters."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 646,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 648,
        "char_start": 468,
        "effective_step": 4,
        "end_token_index": 234,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 235,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: Determine the coordinates of points \\(C\\) and \\(D\\). Assume \\(O\\) is at the origin \\((0,0)\\), then \\(C = (-70\\sqrt{2}, -70\\sqrt{2})\\) and \\(D = (70\\sqrt{2}, -70\\sqrt{2})\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 874,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 876,
        "char_start": 650,
        "effective_step": 5,
        "end_token_index": 306,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 307,
        "step_number": 5,
        "text": "Step 5: Find the coordinates of point \\(P\\) on the line segment \\(CD\\). Let \\(P\\) be at \\((x, -70\\sqrt{2})\\). The distance from \\(H\\) to \\(P\\) will be minimized when \\(P\\) is the foot of the perpendicular from \\(H\\) to \\(CD\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1054,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1055,
        "char_start": 878,
        "effective_step": 6,
        "end_token_index": 372,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 373,
        "step_number": 6,
        "text": "Step 6: Calculate the distance \\(HP\\). The coordinates of \\(H\\) are \\((0, h)\\) for some height \\(h\\). The distance \\(HP\\) is given by:\n\\[ HP = \\sqrt{x^2 + (h + 70\\sqrt{2})^2} \\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1296,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1297,
        "char_start": 1057,
        "effective_step": 7,
        "end_token_index": 470,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 471,
        "step_number": 7,
        "text": "Step 7: Minimize the total length of the new rope \\(HP\\). The minimum occurs when \\(P\\) is the midpoint of \\(CD\\), i.e., \\(P = (0, -70\\sqrt{2})\\). Thus, the distance \\(HP\\) is:\n\\[ HP = \\sqrt{(0)^2 + (h + 70\\sqrt{2})^2} = |h + 70\\sqrt{2}| \\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1420,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1421,
        "char_start": 1299,
        "effective_step": 8,
        "end_token_index": 516,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 517,
        "step_number": 8,
        "text": "Step 8: Calculate the total length of the original ropes \\(HC\\) and \\(HD\\):\n\\[ HC + HD = 150 + 130 = 280 \\text{ meters} \\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1707,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1708,
        "char_start": 1423,
        "effective_step": 9,
        "end_token_index": 613,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 614,
        "step_number": 9,
        "text": "Step 9: Calculate the length of the new rope \\(HP\\). Since \\(P\\) is directly below \\(H\\) on the y-axis, the length of \\(HP\\) is simply the vertical distance from \\(H\\) to \\(O\\) plus the horizontal distance from \\(O\\) to \\(P\\):\n\\[ HP = \\sqrt{(70\\sqrt{2})^2 + h^2} = \\sqrt{9800 + h^2} \\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1817,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1818,
        "char_start": 1710,
        "effective_step": 10,
        "end_token_index": 667,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 668,
        "step_number": 10,
        "text": "Step 10: To minimize \\(HP\\), set \\(h = 0\\):\n\\[ HP = \\sqrt{9800} = 70\\sqrt{2} \\approx 98.99 \\text{ meters} \\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1971,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1972,
        "char_start": 1820,
        "effective_step": 11,
        "end_token_index": 733,
        "near_end": true,
        "prefix_token_count": 734,
        "step_number": 11,
        "text": "Step 11: Calculate the greatest length of rope that can be saved:\n\\[ \\text{Saved length} = 280 - 2 \\times 98.99 = 280 - 197.98 = 82.02 \\text{ meters} \\]"
      }
    ]
